On the twenty-first day of my internship, I started studying processes in Linux. 
I read the relevant sections from the Linux book and learned what a process 
is and how programs are executed by the operating system.

I learned about process IDs, also known as PIDs, and the 
relationship between parent and child processes. I also
studied the ps command and learned how it can be used to 
view information about running processes. In addition,
I looked at the top command to understand how system 
resources and running processes can be monitored.

This topic helped me understand what happens in the 
background when commands and programs are executed in Linux.
I also reviewed the related sections of the Linux 
documentation to reinforce the information from the book.
